WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.230
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.560
All right, I’ll go first!

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.670
Sure!

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.850
How’s that?!

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.510
What is that?
Where’s its face?!

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.990
Oh, come on!
It’s right here!

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.300
This is its face!

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.430
I got this in the bag.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.500
And what do you call <i>that?!</i>
What’s wrong with its <i>body?!</i>

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.690
It’s standing like this!
See?!

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.340
Mine’s definitely better.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.570
No, mine is the best!

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.450
Pikachu, which do you think is better?
Mine or Go’s?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.520
Which looks more like Gaburias?

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.370
Rabbifoot?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.130
Look, Go!

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.670
It’s the ocean!

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:24.970
PocketMonsters

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:27.390
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.970
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.690
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.560
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.900
Be it through fire or through water

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.570
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.070
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.330
Each and every one of my memories

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:54.920
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.840
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.590
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:11.600
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.810
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.150
Let's have a fight!

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.860
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.690
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:26.030
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:32.700
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:38.040
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.540
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.670
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.470
I choose you!

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:55.480
Rabbifoot!
Farewell,

00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:01.490
Mishiro Town, Hoenn Region

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.730
Here we are,
in the Hoenn Region once again!

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.500
Destination: Mishiro Town!

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.870
The Pokémon Center is
right down this road!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.000
Four days here, huh?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.170
We’ve gotta do a thorough job
as research fellows for the Sakuragi Institute!

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.880
Yeah! We’ll watch every second
of the Agehunt’s relaxation!

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.000
Yeah! We’ll study their relaxation patterns
real carefully…

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.260
No, wrong!

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.160
We’re not here for their <i>relaxation!</i>
It’s their <i>migration!</i>

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.380
Really?

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.550
We could see it somewhere along
Mishiro Town’s coastline, right?

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.060
Yeah.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:43.950
Agehunt migration is a rare phenomenon
that can only be observed for a brief time each year.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.030
Study it as carefully as you can!

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.870
In order to find an
easier environment to live in,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.580
they fly thousands of kilometers
together with their kin!

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.890
Isn’t it amazing?

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.490
I’m so excited!

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.750
It’s a Kemusso!

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.640
All right…
Let’s catch it, Rabbifoot!

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.900
I swear… That Rabbifoot…

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.580
Hadn’t you already
caught Kemusso?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.830
Yeah… But I want to evolve one again.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.440
Thank you for having us!

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.780
It’ll be my pleasure.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:26.140
Um, we’re here to study
the Agehunt migration.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.030
Do you know where we should go?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.540
I’m not sure,
since the spot is different each year…

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.890
But the migration always happens on
days when the northern wind is strong.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.040
Northern wind?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.830
I see!
The Agehunt are heading south,

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.760
so they wait for a strong
tailwind from the north to fly!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.340
A headwind would be
more fun, though…

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.750
Maybe for a <i>Sato</i>agehunt…

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.820
What a wind!
But I won’t lose!

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.110
I actually pictured it…

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.650
The ocean sure is wide!
It’s massive!

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:16.080
The wind is blowing
from the Southeast today…

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.100
That’d be a headwind
for the Agehunt.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.070
So no migration?

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.320
Probably not.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.470
But I’m sure they’re
on standby somewhere!

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:30.020
Agehunt! Butterfly Pokémon!
Bug/Flying type!

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:35.480
Its colorfully patterned wings are its most prominent feature,
and its favorite food is the sweet pollen of flowers!

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.890
Pollen of flowers, huh?

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.530
Let’s check over there!

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.400
I-Isn’t that…

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.910
A Zigzaguma!

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.410
Hey, are you okay?

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.540
Hang in there!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.080
It doesn’t look injured…

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.810
It was just fine…

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.690
What was that?

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.000
I’m just glad it wasn’t hurt.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.310
Yeah.

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:28.070
Something wrong,
Rabbifoot?

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.540
Gotta do some research…

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:38.510
Not a single Agehunt
to be found…

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.060
None of the flowers that might have pollen
were in bloom, either.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.620
Where do we look now?

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:47.740
Kemusso!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.970
What? Where?!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:49.470
There!

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.430
I missed it again…

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.400
I wanted to evolve it
into Karasalis…

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.860
Oh, right. All the ones you caught last time
turned into Mayuld.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:03.890
Hang on!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:04.740
Go?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.070
I know… I got it!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.400
Got what?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:14.610
Karasalis!
We should have looked for Karasalis!

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:18.450
I see! Agehunt evolve
from Karasalis…

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.350
…and then they migrate!

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:24.290
All right! Any places nearby
where we might find Karasalis?

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.540
There’s a grove!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.990
Let’s go looking tomorrow!

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:28.460
Yeah!

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.420
I’m so excited,
I’m not sure I can sleep!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.070
Yeah! I’m excited, too!

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.500
Of course!

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.770
Rabbifoot, where were you?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.270
Rabbifoot…

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.670
Delicious! Go, these
Mishiro Croquettes are amazing!

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.670
Go?

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.650
What’s wrong?
You’re not hungry?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.190
Oh, it’s not that…

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.520
Does your stomach hurt?

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:35.130
No, it doesn’t.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.210
There!

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.450
It’s a horde of Karasalis!
We did it, Go!

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:50.360
Yeah! There’ll be
a headwind all day,

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.670
so there’s a high chance
the migration will happen tomorrow!

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.630
Then let’s come check
tomorrow!

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:59.180
I wonder if the Agehunt will fly?
I can’t wait to see!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.910
How about you, Pikachu?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:05.480
Oh, yeah… How do you think
the Karasalis evolve?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.870
I think they go like this…

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:09.320
…and then this!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.690
Oh, like that?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.700
You two really are close…

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.010
Would you like one?

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.550
I think Rabbifoot’s hungry.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.960
Huh?
Didn’t you have breakfast?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.450
Thank you!

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.240
That’s amazing, Rabbifoot…

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.350
You can eat that much?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.250
Hey, can I have one?

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.030
Hey…

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.230
Why?!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:51.080
I get it! I wouldn’t want anyone
asking me for my precious croquettes, either!

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.830
Not even one?

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:53.930
Not a chance!

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:55.030
Oh, come on!

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:58.720
Rabbifoot, I don’t get you!

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:05.370
I don’t know why, but you’ve been acting like this
ever since you evolved!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.490
You don’t follow my lead…
You don’t high-five me…

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:09.790
You don’t even look me in the eyes!

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.930
Will you stop reacting like that?!

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:16.640
Sheesh...!

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:21.050
Do you hate me that much?

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:24.390
Reminds me of my son.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.390
I think your Pokémon’s in
its rebellious phase.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:32.570
Acting all cold and distant every day,
and never being happy with anything you do…

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.440
You just have to give it time.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.430
It just happens at that age.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:39.650
Oh, I see.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:43.740
Rebellious phase?
Just happens at that age?

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:48.370
I see… I see!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.980
You’ve snuck out
two days in a row…

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.490
Where are you going,
and why?

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:29.590
Oh, no… I lost sight of it!

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:33.750
What’s that?

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:37.460
PocketMonsters

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.310
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:43.600
PocketMonsters

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:48.520
Flying
.Bug.
Agehunt
PocketMonsters

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.520
Hurry, hurry!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.570
Go, do we still have time?

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:53.520
Yeah!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.420
But the Northern wind is
getting stronger by the minute!

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:59.820
The migration is starting soon,
no doubt!

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.120
Well?

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.700
They’re evolving!

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.030
A-Awesome!

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.830
This is the Agehunt migration…

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:52.010
Go, are you sure
you don’t want to catch any?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.530
Are <i>you</i> sure
you don’t want to battle them?

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.910
I just feel like…

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:00.630
I know what you mean.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:10.270
The Agehunt migration
was so beautiful!

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.010
Yeah.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:15.270
And we got it all recorded,
so now it’s back home for us tomorrow!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.680
Um, Satoshi…

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.090
Actually…

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.700
It really did leave.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:28.800
Yeah.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.970
I lost sight of it
along the way yesterday.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:34.330
Come on…
You should have said something sooner!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.290
Sorry!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.250
Let’s go!

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.350
H-Huh?

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.860
We lost sight of it again…

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:55.140
I heard this noise
yesterday, too.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.600
Let’s go!

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.900
What is this?

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.220
Look!

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.530
A… A dance?!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.530
Rabbifoot is teaching them
to dance?

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.360
Those apples!

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.920
They’re the ones you bought!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.920
Does this mean…

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:17.230
Has Rabbifoot taken in the Hasubrero and Zigzaguma
as its little brothers?

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.140
Huh? Does that mean Rabbifoot…

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.130
…became the new leader
around here?

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:25.650
It really <i>can</i> smile...

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:31.780
What?

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.060
Is that…?

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:49.670
Dogomb! Loud Voice Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:56.180
It shouts loudly by inhaling air,
and then using its well-developed stomach muscles to exhale!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.580
What’s about to happen?

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.870
They stopped dancing!

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.660
The Dogomb are
throwing off their rhythm!

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.670
Now the Dogomb
have started dancing!

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:50.710
I got it!
This is a dance battle!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.740
They’re fighting over territory
with dance!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:57.600
There’s more than enough food and trees
to survive here.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:01.160
They’re deciding who gets to live here
through a dance battle!

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:05.100
Rabbifoot wants to help
the Hasubrero and Zigzaguma!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:07.160
It wants to help them
dance better!

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:19.260
Don’t let Dogomb’s sound
throw you off!

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.770
Focus on this rhythm!

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:24.270
All right! Us, too!

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:29.970
Now…

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:37.360
Go!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.610
It’s a dance battle, right?

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.800
So let’s dance!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:57.800
Come on!

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:58.010
Go’s late…

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.120
You look so content…

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.860
Farewell, Rabbifoot.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.000
Satoshi.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.340
Go! You’re late…

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.390
Huh? Where’s Rabbifoot?

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.360
I left it behind.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:24.010
What?!
Didn’t you go to pick it up?!

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:26.130
I did…

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.520
But this is for the best.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.770
How is this for the best?!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:35.150
You know how Rabbifoot
has seemed so bored lately, yeah?

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:39.280
It wasn’t because of some rebellious phase…
I’m sure it was all my fault.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:43.580
I think it’ll have a happier life
without me.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.660
Is that really
what you’ve decided?

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.160
Yeah, I’m serious.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:01.760
I won’t stop you
if you’re serious. But…

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.090
Did you tell Rabbifoot?

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.140
Rabbifoot!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.950
Rabbifoot! Rabbifoot!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:39.290
Rabbifoot!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.850
Rabbifoot… Why?

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.330
You smiled…

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:22.970
Okay! I understand!

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.840
Let’s be together!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.780
That’s great, Go!

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:31.220
Yeah! Right, Rabbifoot?

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:36.250
Walking at a slight distance…
Dancing passionately…

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:39.060
Rabbifoot can be quite a handful.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:43.070
But Go wasn’t about to mind
a complicated partner.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.280
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.490
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.990
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.280
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:51.720
Mew!

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.470
Warrgle!

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.260
Runpappa!

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:54.030
Pawou!

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:54.770
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.560
Strike!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.360
Cresselia!

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:57.070
Amakaji!

00:21:57.070 --> 00:21:57.880
Jirachi!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:58.680
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.680 --> 00:21:59.450
Kibago!

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.220
Gonbe!

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.000
Bayleaf!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.500
Freezer!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.690
Zacian!

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:10.140
Shiritori set to Pokémon Techno

